.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-SET 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts set
.Nd change a field of a ticket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts set
.Op Fl m Ar message
.Ar id
.Ar field
.Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command changes a field of an existing ticket.
The
.Ar id
can either be a ticket or a message ID.
.Pp
Fields of the types
.Ql enum ,
.Ql date
and
.Ql number
take a single value.
For
.Ql text
and
.Ql user
fields, all values together form the new value.
For
.Ql set
fields, the values are changes as in the corresponding pseudo-header:
.Ql + Ns Ar value
or just the value adds it,
.Ql - Ns Ar value
removes it, and
.Ql = Ns Ar value
replaces all values.
.Pp
The change is recorded as a message with a pseudo-header.
If the command is run interactively, an editor is invoked where a text can be added to the message.
An invalid value is reported as a warning, but the message is still recorded.
.Pp
The commands
.Nm lbts severity ,
.Nm lbts tags ,
.Nm lbts owner ,
.Nm lbts milestone ,
.Nm lbts deadline
and
.Nm lbts progress
are shortcuts for this command.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl m Ar message
Use the given message instead of invoking an editor.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lbts set 42 priority high
lbts set 42 owner Some One <some@example.org>
lbts set 42 tags patch -moreinfo
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-unset 1 ,
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
